OL,3,GNEWSATeen's family to help water safety
OL,4,Alakes review
OL,5,
OL,6,FLake District authorities have pledged
OL,7,Fto work with the family of a teenager
OL,8,Fwho drowned in a tarn to review water
OL,9,Fsafety measures.
OL,11,FAbsi Ahmed Mohammad, 17 and from
OL,12,FPoulton-le-Fylde in Lancashire, died at
OL,13,FHigh Dam near Windermere on 7 April
OL,14,Fafter suffering cold water shock while
OL,15,Fswimming with friends.
OL,17,FFollowing his inquest, the Lake
OL,18,FDistrict National Park Authority
OL,19,F(LDNPA) said it would review issues
OL,20,Fsuch as signage and the placement of
OL,21,Flife-saving equipment at the end of the
OL,22,Fsummer season.
OL,23,APub: 20-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
